#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""slime - the easy way to drive the slime-farm toolchain.

  ./slime                                   menu: pick a number, answer a few questions
  ./slime gui                               SlimeByte: the app, right in this terminal, with a map

Or straight from the command line (the menu prints these for you as it goes):

  ./slime best-spot --seed S                best farm in YOUR world (10k / 100k / 1M blocks)
  ./slime check --seed S --x X --z Z        one farm: score, best standing height, what it means
  ./slime perimeter --seed S --x X --z Z    commands to build the farm floor in game
  ./slime hunt [--cycles 12]                hunt for a record (stops itself on one)
  ./slime search [--spots main/best_spots.csv]   the exact phase search (needs a spot list)
  ./slime status                            hunt progress so far
  ./slime stop                              stop every hunt process, check the GPU is idle
  ./slime farms [--top 15] [--open N]       your best farms, one table
  ./slime measured --seed S --x X --z Z --ingame N   record a /perimeterinfo reading
  ./slime doctor [--full]                   check your setup, with the fix for anything wrong

  more:  score, y (every standing height), climb, dupes, verify (measurement rig)

Seeds can be typed as text too ("my world") - converted the way Minecraft does.
Add --device N before the command to pick the GPU on a multi-GPU machine.
Nothing here scores anything itself: every number comes from the tools, exactly as before.
"""
